Z||000013||Mach10||09-04-2001||01:24 PM||||My prep-work consisted of running 320 wet grit over the entire car twice, then a 400-grit once. The worst part was the decklid, which was peeling. I sanded that down the to original primer (green?!?). <BR>Took me about 4 hours. Maybe 5? Didn't take more than a rainy afternoon, in anycase. <P>I wouldn't let Maaco do the prep work. As it is, I still have to get some overspray off of some embarrassing areas. But you do get what you pay for. I don't mind. I want to pull my trim off and have it repainted anyway.||||reg||7
